#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Primitives {#primitives}"
msgstr "Primitif {#primitives}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "All physical systems, whether classical or quantum, can exist in different states. For example, a car on a road can have a certain mass, position, speed, or acceleration that characterize its state. Similarly, quantum systems can also have different configurations or states, but they differ from classical systems in how we deal with measurements and state evolution. This leads to unique properties such as *superposition* and *entanglement* that are exclusive to quantum mechanics. Just like we can describe a car's state using physical properties like speed or acceleration, we can also describe the state of a quantum system using *observables*, which are mathematical objects.\n"
msgstr "Semua sistem fisik, baik klasik maupun kuantum, bisa ada dalam keadaan yang berbeda-beda. Misalnya, sebuah mobil di jalan bisa memiliki massa, posisi, kecepatan, atau percepatan tertentu yang mencirikan keadaannya. Demikian pula, sistem kuantum juga bisa memiliki konfigurasi atau keadaan yang berbeda, namun berbeda dari sistem klasik dalam cara kita menangani pengukuran dan evolusi keadaan. Hal ini mengarah pada sifat-sifat unik seperti *superposisi* dan *keterikatan* yang eksklusif untuk mekanika kuantum. Sama seperti kita bisa menggambarkan keadaan mobil menggunakan sifat fisik seperti kecepatan atau percepatan, kita juga bisa menggambarkan keadaan sistem kuantum menggunakan *observabel*, yang merupakan objek matematis.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In quantum mechanics, states are represented by normalized complex column vectors, or *kets* ($|\\psi\\rangle$), and observables are Hermitian linear operators ($\\hat{H}=\\hat{H}^{\\dagger}$) that act on the kets. An eigenvector ($|\\lambda\\rangle$) of an observable is known as an *eigenstate*. Measuring an observable for one of its eigenstates ($|\\lambda\\rangle$) will give us the corresponding eigenvalue ($\\lambda$) as readout.\n"
msgstr "Dalam mekanika kuantum, keadaan direpresentasikan oleh vektor kolom kompleks yang dinormalisasi, atau *ket* ($|\\psi\\rangle$), dan observabel adalah operator linear Hermitian ($\\hat{H}=\\hat{H}^{\\dagger}$) yang bekerja pada ket. Vektor eigen ($|\\lambda\\rangle$) dari sebuah observabel dikenal sebagai *eigenstate*. Mengukur observabel untuk salah satu eigenstate-nya ($|\\lambda\\rangle$) akan memberikan nilai eigen yang sesuai ($\\lambda$) sebagai hasil baca.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If you're wondering how to measure a quantum system and what you can measure, Qiskit offers two <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Basic and fundamental operations or data type. Qiskit has the Sampler and Estimator primitives to serve as building blocks to easily construct complex algorithmic workloads.\">primitives</DefinitionTooltip> that can help:\n"
msgstr "Jika kamu bertanya-tanya bagaimana cara mengukur sistem kuantum dan apa yang bisa kamu ukur, Qiskit menawarkan dua <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Basic and fundamental operations or data type. Qiskit has the Sampler and Estimator primitives to serve as building blocks to easily construct complex algorithmic workloads.\">primitif</DefinitionTooltip> yang bisa membantu:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`Sampler`: Given a quantum state $|\\psi\\rangle$, this primitive obtains the probability of each possible computational basis state.\n"
msgstr "`Sampler`: Diberikan keadaan kuantum $|\\psi\\rangle$, primitif ini mendapatkan probabilitas dari setiap kemungkinan keadaan basis komputasional.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`Estimator`: Given a quantum observable $\\hat{H}$ and a state $|\\psi\\rangle$, this primitive computes the expected value of $\\hat{H}$.\n"
msgstr "`Estimator`: Diberikan observabel kuantum $\\hat{H}$ dan keadaan $|\\psi\\rangle$, primitif ini menghitung nilai ekspektasi dari $\\hat{H}$.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Sampler primitive {#the-sampler-primitive}"
msgstr "Primitif Sampler {#the-sampler-primitive}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `Sampler` primitive calculates the probability of obtaining each possible state $|k\\rangle$ from the computational basis, given a quantum circuit that prepares the state $|\\psi\\rangle$. It calculates\n"
msgstr "Primitif `Sampler` menghitung probabilitas mendapatkan setiap kemungkinan keadaan $|k\\rangle$ dari basis komputasional, diberikan sebuah sirkuit kuantum yang mempersiapkan keadaan $|\\psi\\rangle$. Ia menghitung\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"p_k = |\\langle k | \\psi \\rangle|^2 \\quad \\forall k \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^n \\equiv \\{0,1,\\cdots,2^n-1\\},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"p_k = |\\langle k | \\psi \\rangle|^2 \\quad \\forall k \\in \\mathbb{Z}_2^n \\equiv \\{0,1,\\cdots,2^n-1\\},\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Where $n$ is the number of qubits, and $k$ the integer representation of any possible output binary string $\\{0,1\\}^n$ (that is, integers base $2$).\n"
msgstr "Di mana $n$ adalah jumlah qubit, dan $k$ representasi integer dari semua kemungkinan string biner output $\\{0,1\\}^n$ (yaitu, bilangan bulat basis $2$).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "The Qiskit Runtime [`Sampler`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/sampler-v2) runs the circuit multiple times on a quantum device, performing measurements on each run, and reconstructing the probability distribution from the recovered bitstrings. The more runs (or *shots*) it performs, the more accurate the results will be, but this requires more time and quantum resources.\n"
msgid "The IBM Quantum [`Sampler`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/sampler-v2) runs the circuit multiple times on a quantum device, performing measurements on each run, and reconstructing the probability distribution from the recovered bitstrings. The more runs (or *shots*) it performs, the more accurate the results will be, but this requires more time and quantum resources.\n"
msgstr "Qiskit Runtime [`Sampler`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/sampler-v2) menjalankan Circuit beberapa kali pada perangkat kuantum, melakukan pengukuran pada setiap jalannya, dan merekonstruksi distribusi probabilitas dari bitstring yang didapatkan. Semakin banyak jalannya (atau *shot*), semakin akurat hasilnya, namun ini membutuhkan lebih banyak waktu dan sumber daya kuantum.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "However, since the number of possible outputs grows exponentially with the number of qubits $n$ (that is, $2^n$), the number of shots will need to grow exponentially as well in order to capture a _dense_ probability distribution. Therefore, `Sampler` is only efficient for *sparse* probability distributions; where the target state $|\\psi\\rangle$ must be expressible as a linear combination of the computational basis states, with the number of terms growing at most polynomially with the number of qubits:\n"
msgstr "Namun, karena jumlah kemungkinan output tumbuh secara eksponensial seiring dengan jumlah qubit $n$ (yaitu, $2^n$), jumlah shot juga perlu tumbuh secara eksponensial agar bisa menangkap distribusi probabilitas yang _padat_. Oleh karena itu, `Sampler` hanya efisien untuk distribusi probabilitas yang *jarang*; di mana keadaan target $|\\psi\\rangle$ harus bisa diekspresikan sebagai kombinasi linear dari keadaan basis komputasional, dengan jumlah suku yang tumbuh paling banyak secara polinomial seiring dengan jumlah qubit:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle = \\sum^{\\text{Poly}(n)}_k w_k |k\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle = \\sum^{\\text{Poly}(n)}_k w_k |k\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `Sampler` can also be configured to retrieve probabilities from a subsection of the circuit, representing a subset of the total possible states.\n"
msgstr "`Sampler` juga bisa dikonfigurasi untuk mengambil probabilitas dari sebagian Circuit, yang merepresentasikan subset dari total kemungkinan keadaan.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Estimator primitive {#the-estimator-primitive}"
msgstr "Primitif Estimator {#the-estimator-primitive}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `Estimator` primitive calculates the expectation value of an observable $\\hat{H}$ for a quantum state $|\\psi\\rangle$; where the observable probabilities can be expressed as $p_\\lambda = |\\langle\\lambda|\\psi\\rangle|^2$, being $|\\lambda\\rangle$ the eigenstates of the observable $\\hat{H}$. The expectation value is then defined as the average of all possible outcomes $\\lambda$ (that is, the eigenvalues of the observable) of a measurement of the state $|\\psi\\rangle$, weighted by the corresponding probabilities:\n"
msgstr "Primitif `Estimator` menghitung nilai ekspektasi dari observabel $\\hat{H}$ untuk keadaan kuantum $|\\psi\\rangle$; di mana probabilitas observabel bisa diekspresikan sebagai $p_\\lambda = |\\langle\\lambda|\\psi\\rangle|^2$, dengan $|\\lambda\\rangle$ adalah eigenstate dari observabel $\\hat{H}$. Nilai ekspektasi kemudian didefinisikan sebagai rata-rata dari semua kemungkinan hasil $\\lambda$ (yaitu, nilai eigen dari observabel) dari sebuah pengukuran keadaan $|\\psi\\rangle$, berbobot oleh probabilitas yang sesuai:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle\\hat{H}\\rangle_\\psi := \\sum_\\lambda p_\\lambda \\lambda = \\langle \\psi | \\hat{H} | \\psi \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle\\hat{H}\\rangle_\\psi := \\sum_\\lambda p_\\lambda \\lambda = \\langle \\psi | \\hat{H} | \\psi \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "However, calculating the expectation value of an observable is not always possible, as we often don't know its eigenbasis. The Qiskit Runtime [`Estimator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/estimator-v2) uses a complex algebraic process to estimate the expectation value on a real quantum device by breaking down the observable into a combination of other observables whose eigenbasis we do know.\n"
msgid "However, calculating the expectation value of an observable is not always possible, as we often don't know its eigenbasis. The IBM Quantum [`Estimator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/estimator-v2) uses a complex algebraic process to estimate the expectation value on a real quantum device by breaking down the observable into a combination of other observables whose eigenbasis we do know.\n"
msgstr "Namun, menghitung nilai ekspektasi dari sebuah observabel tidak selalu bisa dilakukan, karena kita sering tidak mengetahui eigenbasis-nya. Qiskit Runtime [`Estimator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/estimator-v2) menggunakan proses aljabar yang kompleks untuk memperkirakan nilai ekspektasi pada perangkat kuantum nyata dengan menguraikan observabel menjadi kombinasi dari observabel lain yang eigenbasis-nya sudah kita ketahui.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In simpler terms, `Estimator` breaks down any observable that it doesn't know how to measure into simpler, measurable observables called <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Set of matrices commonly used in quantum computing to represent and manipulate quantum states, consisting of the identity matrix and the three Pauli matrices (X, Y, and Z).\">Pauli operators</DefinitionTooltip>.\n"
"Any operator can be expressed as a combination of $4^n$ Pauli operators.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam istilah yang lebih sederhana, `Estimator` menguraikan setiap observabel yang tidak diketahui cara mengukurnya menjadi observabel yang lebih sederhana dan bisa diukur yang disebut <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Set of matrices commonly used in quantum computing to represent and manipulate quantum states, consisting of the identity matrix and the three Pauli matrices (X, Y, and Z).\">operator Pauli</DefinitionTooltip>.\n"
"Setiap operator bisa diekspresikan sebagai kombinasi dari $4^n$ operator Pauli.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{P}_k :=\n"
"\\sigma_{k_{n-1}}\\otimes \\cdots \\otimes \\sigma_{k_0} \\quad\n"
"\\forall k \\in \\mathbb{Z}_4^n \\equiv \\{0,1,\\cdots,4^n-1\\}, \\\\\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{P}_k :=\n"
"\\sigma_{k_{n-1}}\\otimes \\cdots \\otimes \\sigma_{k_0} \\quad\n"
"\\forall k \\in \\mathbb{Z}_4^n \\equiv \\{0,1,\\cdots,4^n-1\\}, \\\\\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "such that\n"
msgstr "sehingga\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{H} = \\sum^{4^n-1}_{k=0} w_k \\hat{P}_k\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat{H} = \\sum^{4^n-1}_{k=0} w_k \\hat{P}_k\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $n$ is the number of qubits, $k \\equiv k_{n-1} \\cdots k_0$ for $k_l \\in \\mathbb{Z}_4 \\equiv \\{0, 1, 2, 3\\}$ (that is, integers base $4$), and $(\\sigma_0, \\sigma_1, \\sigma_2, \\sigma_3) := (I, X, Y, Z)$.\n"
msgstr "di mana $n$ adalah jumlah qubit, $k \\equiv k_{n-1} \\cdots k_0$ untuk $k_l \\in \\mathbb{Z}_4 \\equiv \\{0, 1, 2, 3\\}$ (yaitu, bilangan bulat basis $4$), dan $(\\sigma_0, \\sigma_1, \\sigma_2, \\sigma_3) := (I, X, Y, Z)$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "After performing this decomposition, `Estimator` derives a new circuit $V_k|\\psi\\rangle$ for each observable $\\hat{P}_k$ (from the original circuit), to effectively *diagonalize* the Pauli observable in the computational basis and measure it. We can easily measure Pauli observables because we know $V_k$ ahead of time, which is not the case generally for other observables.\n"
msgstr "Setelah melakukan dekomposisi ini, `Estimator` menghasilkan Circuit baru $V_k|\\psi\\rangle$ untuk setiap observabel $\\hat{P}_k$ (dari Circuit asli), untuk secara efektif *mendiagonalisasi* observabel Pauli dalam basis komputasional dan mengukurnya. Kita bisa dengan mudah mengukur observabel Pauli karena kita mengetahui $V_k$ sebelumnya, yang tidak demikian halnya untuk observabel lain pada umumnya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For each $\\hat{P}_{k}$, the `Estimator` runs the corresponding circuit on a quantum device multiple times, measures the output state in the computational basis, and calculates the probability $p_{kj}$ of obtaining each possible output $j$. It then looks for the eigenvalue $\\lambda_{kj}$ of $P_k$ corresponding to each output $j$, multiplies by $w_k$, and adds all the results together to obtain the expected value of the observable $\\hat{H}$ for the given state $|\\psi\\rangle$.\n"
msgstr "Untuk setiap $\\hat{P}_{k}$, `Estimator` menjalankan Circuit yang sesuai pada perangkat kuantum beberapa kali, mengukur keadaan output dalam basis komputasional, dan menghitung probabilitas $p_{kj}$ untuk mendapatkan setiap kemungkinan output $j$. Kemudian ia mencari nilai eigen $\\lambda_{kj}$ dari $P_k$ yang sesuai dengan setiap output $j$, mengalikannya dengan $w_k$, dan menjumlahkan semua hasilnya untuk mendapatkan nilai ekspektasi dari observabel $\\hat{H}$ untuk keadaan $|\\psi\\rangle$ yang diberikan.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle\\hat{H}\\rangle_\\psi =\n"
"\\sum_{k=0}^{4^n-1} w_k \\sum_{j=0}^{2^n-1}p_{kj} \\lambda_{kj},\n"
"$$\n"
"Since calculating the expectation value of $4^n$ Paulis is impractical (that is, exponentially growing), `Estimator` can only be efficient when a large amount of $w_k$ are zero (that is, *sparse* Pauli decomposition instead of *dense*). Formally we say that, for this computation to be *efficiently solvable*, the number of non-zero terms has to grow at most polynomially with the number of qubits $n$: $\\hat{H} = \\sum^{\\text{Poly}(n)}_k w_k \\hat{P}_k$.\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle\\hat{H}\\rangle_\\psi =\n"
"\\sum_{k=0}^{4^n-1} w_k \\sum_{j=0}^{2^n-1}p_{kj} \\lambda_{kj},\n"
"$$\n"
"Karena menghitung nilai ekspektasi dari $4^n$ Pauli tidak praktis (yaitu, tumbuh secara eksponensial), `Estimator` hanya bisa efisien ketika sejumlah besar $w_k$ bernilai nol (yaitu, dekomposisi Pauli yang *jarang* bukan yang *padat*). Secara formal kita katakan bahwa, agar komputasi ini bisa *diselesaikan secara efisien*, jumlah suku yang tidak nol harus tumbuh paling banyak secara polinomial seiring dengan jumlah qubit $n$: $\\hat{H} = \\sum^{\\text{Poly}(n)}_k w_k \\hat{P}_k.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The reader may notice the implicit assumption that probability <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The process of taking several measurements of one or several things.\">sampling</DefinitionTooltip> also needs to be efficient as explained for `Sampler`, which means\n"
msgstr "Pembaca mungkin memperhatikan asumsi implisit bahwa <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The process of taking several measurements of one or several things.\">pengambilan sampel</DefinitionTooltip> probabilitas juga perlu efisien seperti yang dijelaskan untuk `Sampler`, yang berarti\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle\\hat{H}\\rangle_\\psi =\n"
"\\sum_{k}^{\\text{Poly}(n)} w_k \\sum_{j}^{\\text{Poly}(n)}p_{kj} \\lambda_{kj}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle\\hat{H}\\rangle_\\psi =\n"
"\\sum_{k}^{\\text{Poly}(n)} w_k \\sum_{j}^{\\text{Poly}(n)}p_{kj} \\lambda_{kj}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Guided example to calculate expectation values {#guided-example-to-calculate-expectation-values}"
msgstr "Contoh terpandu untuk menghitung nilai ekspektasi {#guided-example-to-calculate-expectation-values}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Let's assume the single-qubit state $|+\\rangle := H|0\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle + |1\\rangle)$, and observable\n"
msgstr "Mari kita asumsikan keadaan qubit tunggal $|+\\rangle := H|0\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(|0\\rangle + |1\\rangle)$, dan observabel\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\hat{H}\n"
"& = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"-1 & 2 \\\\\n"
"2 & 1 \\\\\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"& = 2X - Z\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\hat{H}\n"
"& = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"-1 & 2 \\\\\n"
"2 & 1 \\\\\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"& = 2X - Z\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "with the following theoretical expectation value $\\langle\\hat{H}\\rangle_+ = \\langle+|\\hat{H}|+\\rangle = 2$.\n"
msgstr "dengan nilai ekspektasi teoritis berikut $\\langle\\hat{H}\\rangle_+ = \\langle+|\\hat{H}|+\\rangle = 2$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Since we do not know how to measure this observable, we cannot compute its expectation value directly, and we need to re-express it as $\\langle\\hat{H}\\rangle_+ = 2\\langle X \\rangle_+ - \\langle Z \\rangle_+ $. Which can be shown to evaluate to the same result by virtue of noting that $\\langle+|X|+\\rangle = 1$, and $\\langle+|Z|+\\rangle = 0$.\n"
msgstr "Karena kita tidak tahu cara mengukur observabel ini, kita tidak bisa menghitung nilai ekspektasinya secara langsung, dan kita perlu mengekspresikannya kembali sebagai $\\langle\\hat{H}\\rangle_+ = 2\\langle X \\rangle_+ - \\langle Z \\rangle_+ $. Yang bisa ditunjukkan menghasilkan hasil yang sama dengan memperhatikan bahwa $\\langle+|X|+\\rangle = 1$, dan $\\langle+|Z|+\\rangle = 0$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Let see how to compute $\\langle X \\rangle_+$ and $\\langle Z \\rangle_+$ directly. Since $X$ and $Z$ do not commute (that is, they don't share the same eigenbasis), they cannot be measured simultaneously, therefore we need the auxiliary circuits:\n"
msgstr "Mari kita lihat cara menghitung $\\langle X \\rangle_+$ dan $\\langle Z \\rangle_+$ secara langsung. Karena $X$ dan $Z$ tidak komutatif (yaitu, mereka tidak berbagi eigenbasis yang sama), mereka tidak bisa diukur secara bersamaan, sehingga kita memerlukan Circuit bantu:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
